[l_english.STATE_LORE_203]
Chuan Du, meaning “the capital in the mountains” in Kirinese. Similar to the stories of other Kirin civilizations, there was once a Kirin tribe that survived the Nirik Rebellion and established a city-state here. This city-state gradually prospered under the efforts of several generations of Kirins.
Located among the mountains, the Chuan Du civilization had almost no contact with the outside world. As the civilization prospered, the number of Kirins increased, but the arable land was limited, and the fate of the Chuan Du civilization was inevitable. After the flames, only some porcelain remains to tell the glory of this civilization.

[l_simp_chinese.STATE_LORE_203]
川都，麒麟语中“山中的首都”之意。与其他麒麟文明的故事差不多，历史上曾有一支从逆麟之乱中幸存的麒麟部族在这里建立了一座城邦。这座城邦在几代麒麟的努力下逐渐繁荣起来。
由于在群山之中，川都文明与外界几乎没有联系。随着文明的繁荣，麒口数量的增长，而耕地却有限，川都文明的结局便也不可避免，烈火后，只剩下一些瓷器诉说着这个文明曾经的辉煌。
